## Why This Is Asked
This question tests understanding of fundamental thread synchronization primitives, blocking behavior, and race-condition avoidance in practical concurrent data structures. It demonstrates a candidate's ability to implement classic producer-consumer patterns safely.

## Key Concepts
- **Circular buffer:** Fixed-capacity queue using modulo arithmetic for wraparound
- **Mutual exclusion:** Single mutex protecting all shared state (head, tail, count)
- **Blocking semantics:** Condition variables to suspend threads when queue is full/empty
- **Spurious wakeups:** Why `wait()` must be called with a predicate in a while loop
- **Fairness:** FIFO ordering from condition variable wakeups and serialized mutex access

## Code Example
```cpp
#include <mutex>
#include <condition_variable>
#include <vector>

template<typename T>
class BoundedBlockingQueue {
  static constexpr size_t N = 1024;
  std::vector<T> buf_{N};
  size_t head_ = 0, tail_ = 0, count_ = 0;
  std::mutex mutex_;
  std::condition_variable not_full_, not_empty_;

public:
  void push(T item) {
    std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
    not_full_.wait(lock, [this] { return count_ < N; });
    buf_[tail_] = std::move(item);
    tail_ = (tail_ + 1) % N;
    ++count_;
    not_empty_.notify_one();
  }

  T pop() {
    std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
    not_empty_.wait(lock, [this] { return count_ > 0; });
    T item = std::move(buf_[head_]);
    head_ = (head_ + 1) % N;
    --count_;
    not_full_.notify_one();
    return item;
  }
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of transactional memory in real workloads, careful fallback design, and low-latency queues.

## Key Concepts
- Intel TSX (_xbegin/_xend)
- CAS-based fallback paths
- Per-slot sequence counters to avoid ABA
- Cache-line alignment and false sharing avoidance
- Microbenchmarking for latency and throughput

## Code Example
```c
// Skeleton TSX-based enqueue
typedef struct { unsigned long long seq; unsigned long long val; } slot_t;
typedef struct { slot_t *slots; unsigned head, tail, cap; } q_t;
static inline int enqueue_htm(q_t *q, unsigned long long val) {
    unsigned pos = q->tail;
    if ((pos + 1) % q->cap == q->head) return -1; // full

    unsigned status = _xbegin();
    if (status == _XBEGIN_STARTED) {
        q->slots[pos].val = val;
        q->slots[pos].seq = pos + 1;
        q->tail = (pos + 1) % q->cap;
        _xend();
        return 0;
    }

    // Fallback: CAS-based enqueue with sequence validation
    return enqueue_cas(q, val);
}
```

## Design Considerations
- Retry limits: 3-5 TSX attempts before permanent fallback
- Alignment: 64-byte cache line boundaries
- Contention handling: exponential backoff in fallback path
- Benchmark: measure 99th percentile latency under 1 vs 16 producer/consumer pairs

